1
00:03:25,384 --> 00:03:31,384
Damned be the ties that bind

2
00:06:50,769 --> 00:06:56,769
The Atoning is a drama, horror, thriller film directed by Michael Williams.

3
00:10:16,153 --> 00:10:22,153
Vera, Ray, and Sam, a seemingly normal family, are
haunted by more than mere ghosts.

4
00:13:41,538 --> 00:13:47,538
The lingering horror of their past threatens their ability to function as a
loving family until they become enlightened by a mystical encounter.

5
00:17:06,923 --> 00:17:12,923
From that moment on, they're thrust into a horror worse
than anything they've ever experienced.

6
00:20:32,307 --> 00:20:38,307
Personal demons manifest and tear the family apart from the
inside out as they come to terms with their past.

7
00:23:57,692 --> 00:24:03,692
Sam, played by Cannon Bosarge.

8
00:27:23,076 --> 00:27:29,076
Ray, played by Michael LaCour.

9
00:30:48,461 --> 00:30:54,461
Vera, played by Virginia Newcomb.

10
00:34:13,846 --> 00:34:19,846
Charon Lilith, played by Dorothy Weems.

11
00:37:39,230 --> 00:37:45,230
Sarah, played by Sherri Eakin.

12
00:41:04,615 --> 00:41:10,615
Julie, played by Ashlyn Jade Lopez.

13
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:36,000
Atonement is a 2007 romantic war tragedy film directed by Joe Wright and starring James
McAvoy, Keira Knightley, Saoirse Ronan, Romola Garai, and Vanessa Redgrave.

14
00:47:55,384 --> 00:48:01,384
It is based on the 2001 novel by Ian McEwan.

15
00:51:20,769 --> 00:51:26,769
The film chronicles a crime and its consequences over
six decades, beginning in the 1930s.

16
00:54:46,153 --> 00:54:52,153
It was produced for StudioCanal and filmed in England.

17
00:58:11,538 --> 00:58:17,538
Distributed in most of the world by Universal Studios, it was released theatrically in the United Kingdom
on 7 September 2007 and in North America exactly three months later on 7 December 2007.

18
01:01:36,923 --> 01:01:42,923
Atonement opened both the 2007 Vancouver International Film
Festival and the 64th Venice International Film Festival.

19
01:05:02,307 --> 01:05:08,307
Wright, at age 35, was the youngest director ever to open the Venice event.

20
01:08:27,692 --> 01:08:33,692
The film was a commercial success and earned a worldwide gross of
approximately $129 million against a budget of $30 million.

21
01:11:53,076 --> 01:11:59,076
Critics praised its acting, emotional depth, Wright's direction, Dario Marianelli's score, the
cinematography, editing, visuals, and the film's incorporation of historic events.

22
01:15:18,461 --> 01:15:24,461
Among numerous accolades, Atonement was nominated in seven categories at the 80th Academy Awards, including Best
Picture, Best Supporting Actress (for Ronan), Best Adapted Screenplay, and Best Original Score, which it won.

23
01:18:43,846 --> 01:18:49,846
It also garnered fourteen nominations at the 61st British Academy Film Awards, winning both Best Film
and Production Design; and won the Golden Globe Award for Best Motion Picture – Drama.

24
01:22:09,230 --> 01:22:15,230
The film explores themes of infidelity, afterlife, supernatural, puzzle, murder.

25
01:25:34,615 --> 01:25:40,615
The tone is dark and lighthearted and emotional.
